# Low-disk probe (local-maintenance, sd:10426): every 15 minutes, sample
# free space once per filesystem the maintenance conf's disk| lines name.
# Healthy, it prints that and stops. Below a threshold it runs only the
# safe cleanup, under maintenance-nightly's lock, and records free bytes
# before and after; still low, the run's report needs attention.
JOB_SCHEDULE="*/15 * * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="45m"
JOB_COMMAND="sh \"$ROOT/../local-maintenance/maintenance.sh\" probe"
